  "worked_solution": "Since $f(x)$ is left-continuous at $x=-9,$ we must have\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to (-9)^{-}}f(x)=f(-9)=4.\n$$\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (-9)^{-}}(f(x)-x)^{2}=(4-(-9))^{2}=169.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
